! QED arm: FSR -- photon radiation off the OUTGOING lepton only.
!
! The scattered lepton is what Q2, x and y are reconstructed from, so a photon
! radiated before reconstruction moves the event in the fiducial variables
! themselves.  This is the arm that migrates events across the Q2 > 4 GeV2 and
! 0.2 < y < 0.9 boundaries, and it exists in BOTH currents: the charged
! current's outgoing lepton is a muon.
TimeShower:QEDshowerByL = on
